      "id": "assertion-message-matches",
      "kind": "noul",
      "ask": "When this check fails, its message ($MSG) tells the reader something untrue about what was wrong, judged against the condition ($COND) that was actually tested.",
      "note": "The check fires when the guard is true for if-throw shapes and when the condition is false for assert and invariant shapes; judge the message against the case in which it is shown. Only the condition and the message are compared; whether the check itself is correct is not the question. A throw inside a test double -- a fake, stub, mock, replaced global or scripted dependency whose body returns canned responses for a test -- is not a check on the program's state and is out of scope: its condition picks when the scripted failure happens, such as a call counter, a route or an input id, and its message names the failure the test is simulating. Such a message describes the scenario, not the condition, and is not a violation. When the matched check is the inner guard of a nested condition and the inner condition only chooses between messages, the outer condition is what failed, and the message is judged against it.",
      "draft": "f7e31d13f6dc",
      "at": 0.65,
      "state": "local",
      "subject": "node",
      "severity": "warning",
      "language": "TypeScript"
    }
